@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# Actual R1 fixture cold review
+
+PASS for ACTUAL_R1_DERIVATION SHA ddcf0e7425c1c81c84a79ccbb7c443c311ddef37d2c53269281760c0072e7ef9 and inspected actual_r1_check.py (27c764 prefix). Full proof and polynomial Haar implementation read; I independently recomputed the rational excess rather than rerunning the entire author checker. The author's22 first-run checks remain author evidence, not an independently repeated engine run.
+
+At bivalent vertices the full neutral R1 spin-network basis is indeed1,chi,bar chi: the unique intertwiner forces a single consistent loop irrep, and only0,3,bar3 are retained. Its kinetic energies0,16,16 and J offdiagonal1/6 follow from fundamental fusion, including the determinant invariant for the chi/bar coupling. The symmetric-sector eigenvector equation gives v=96t/(1+t-2t²); the other symmetric and antisymmetric eigenvalues match the source. Since the stipulated eigenvalue is below4, positivity of compressed V and K>=4 on the orthogonal complement of the global vacuum exclude every nonneutral gauge sector. This establishes the full-carrier premise rather than assuming it from a constrained minimum.
+
+The projection formulas have the correct indices. Projection of U_ij U_kl is its antisymmetric component(1/2)epsilon_ika epsilon_jlb bar U_ab. Projection of U_ij bar U_kl is delta_ik delta_jl/3, giving C_ij=bar M_ji/3. M may be Haar-collapsed for integrals because it is the product of three independent links, but its three separate kinetic contributions must remain counted; the source does so. The A/B/C patterns have energies4,16,12 and are pairwise orthogonal by their distinct link irreps.
+
+The actual polynomial integrator pairs matching row and column indices in the one-fundamental/one-antifundamental Haar rule, handles the three-factor epsilon rule with1/6, and throws on unsupported balanced moments. It does not silently discard unknown moments. Its matrix norm includes the required1/3 color trace. The displayed Gram and magnetic matrices then give qnum=1+4t²/9, jnum=(4t+t²)/27 and kinetic numerator4+20t²/3. These contractions are exact retained-state matrix elements of the compressed face, not a toy Hamiltonian.
+
+Independent rational recomputation at t=1/100, v=1600/1683 gives Delta=454685351/113607549 and Delta-4=255155/113607549>0. The norm loss is7/45009. Thus the failure of copying the exact full-unitary4 energy identity is real for this trial; it is not a statement about the charged spectral minimum. The actual-energy theta and rational square-root bounds satisfy the general theorem, whereas the crude8v/4 budget exceeds1. Preserving this latter failure instead of retuning is scientifically appropriate. No new coupling-window threshold or full-volume conclusion follows from the fixture. No correction requested.
diff --git a/.claude/science/physics-loops/finite-pw-charged-upper-20260907/evidence/primary_review/REVIEW.md b/.claude/science/physics-loops/finite-pw-charged-upper-20260907/evidence/primary_review/REVIEW.md
