index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..e807ffcb2bc409723d6f3cdb09ce2a4ec7989a86
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.claude/science/physics-loops/finite-pw-charged-upper-20260907/evidence/primary_review/REVIEW.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# Independent block42 cold review
+
+Native mathematical PASS for DERIVATION SHA55f5a4e94d945cc30ad2d00718378e0f92559106bd94039c40cbfc55dc59955d. Root224fa648db011ab7f22011949279e523f04cf0d436cbbf1694e91a507dfc8129 requires one explicit generator-normalization correction before PASS; all subsequent estimates agree with the consistent native convention. Both complete proofs read independently after their freezes. No source edits.
+
+## Required root correction
+
+Root Section3 states Tr(T_A T_B)=2delta_AB together with sum_(A=1)^8 T_A²=(8/3)I_3. These cannot both hold: tracing the sum gives16 on the first convention and8 on the second. The stated K normalization, fundamental energy4/a and every displayed derivative coefficient use Tr(T_A T_B)=delta_AB, as native explicitly states. Change the root trace normalization to delta_AB, preserving the Casimir8/3 and all coefficients. This is a convention repair, not a fitted or substantive change to the proven bound. Do not instead retain Tr2 and silently keep the same Laplacian.
+
+## Full-carrier local budget
+
+The mixed replacement is legitimate precisely on the full finite tensor carrier. It retains all reduced expectations away from one link, sets that link's kinetic energy to zero, and changes at most four positive face terms by at most2v each. Thus E_e<=8v follows from global full-carrier minimality. The replacement is not generally Gauss-invariant; both proofs explicitly explain why a merely physical-sector minimizer would not justify this step. Neutrality is an additional property of the full ground, supplied in the existing weak window. A boundary singlet projection is not inserted.
+
+## Charged norm and kinetic form
+
+C=PWP equals the distinct-link compressed product and retains covariance. Matrix Hilbert–Schmidt norm Tr/3 is the normalized nine-component source convention, not an arbitrary reference-color state. Subtraction of the same E0 before estimates makes the exact Rayleigh numerator <CΩ,[H_R,C]Ω>; no extensive E0 normalization term remains.
+
+Finite PW functions and their finite-word products are smooth, so the commutators have actual operator-domain meaning. With the consistent Tr1 convention, each differentiated path factor has generator insertion, sum_A T_A²=8I/3, and the row norm squared is8d/3 pointwise. The scalar derivative norm is(2a/3)E_path. Their product with3/a gives4sqrt(d E_path/a), as claimed. The exact full kinetic matrix trace has zero cross terms by tracelessness, including complex Ω and reversed link orientation. It gives4d/a. Projecting loses the pairing with QWΩ and an explicitly controlled derivative vector; this is a genuine form-energy estimate rather than a misuse of norm convergence.
+
+## Local compressed magnetic error
+
+A face with no common link commutes with C exactly, since it is color-scalar. The compression identity has correct signs: [PVP,PWP]=PWQVP-PVQWP. On retained inputs QV_f annihilates the four-link interior by the actual fundamental/conjugate face fusion rule. The union of top-shell projections is commuting, with probability at most E_face/e_R. Hence ||QV_fΩ||<=2v sqrt(E_face/e_R). The second term costs2v sqrt(theta); ||CΩ||<=1 suffices in the Rayleigh pairing. At most4d touching faces contribute, independent of ambient volume. Scalar potential parts create no leakage.
+
+## Result and limits
+
+Replacing q by1-theta is safe because the actual numerator is nonnegative under the full-ground premise, and the explicit upper numerator is nonnegative. The dimensionless and dimensionful versions match exactly. For fixed a,v,d the denominator tends to1 and all displayed corrections vanish asR^-1, uniformly in ambient graphs with the stated incidence and full-ground premise. At v0 the vacuum has zero shell energy and exact path action forR>=1. Native's relative growing-d qualification h_R/d tending to infinity is also sufficient at fixed av. Neither proof claims uniformity in arbitrary d at fixed cutoff.
+
+No finite-hardware realization, deterministic compression, source-minimum infinite-volume convergence or new charged lower bound is inferred. Subject to the root normalization correction above, no further mathematical gap found.
