+# Prospective actual single-plaquette R1 fixture
+
+2026-09-07 about21:47UTC, before numerical/exact checker execution. Take a=1, four-link cycle, R=1 and the actual SU3 Wilson face. Gauge-invariant neutral functions are exactly span{1,chi_3,chi_bar3}; all link representations around the bivalent cycle must match. Character fusion predicts J has zero diagonal and off-diagonal1/6. K is diag(0,16,16). Set t=1/100 and v=96t/(1+t-2t^2), fixed prospectively; the normalized state proportional to1+t(chi+bar chi) should be the lowest eigenvector. Its energy E0=v-vt/3 lies below v<4, whereas all nontrivial gauge sectors have K>=4 and nonnegative compressed V, so it is also the full-carrier ground.
+
+For a single-link transporter W, let A=W, B=P(W chi), C=P(W bar chi). Actual SU3 Haar projection formulas should give mutually orthogonal squared norms1,1/3,1/9; kinetic energies4,16,12 respectively. Anticipated unnormalized J matrix has AB=1/18, AC=1/54, BC=1/54 and zero diagonal. Derive these from explicit Kronecker/epsilon contractions, not by installing the expected coefficients. In variables U for the path link and M for the product of the other three links, B_ij=(1/2)sum eps(i,k,a)eps(j,l,b)bar U_ab M_lk and C_ij=bar M_ji/3. Both full Haar factors are independent; degree and support identify the actual cutoff and electric energies on all four links.
+
+Check exact trial norm, kinetic and potential Rayleigh quotient, positive finite-cutoff deviation above4 if present, and the actual-energy version of42. The crude sufficient bound theta_bar=8v/e_R may exceed1 for this fixed fixture; preserve that failure of a sufficient bound rather than retuning v. Include adverse incorrect source normalization, wrong fusion/projection coefficients, and the volume-sized naive energy penalty that42 avoids. This is one actual finite model, not a numerical proof of volume-uniform convergence or a critical-coupling estimate.
