+# Root42 prospective energy-form bridge
+
+2026-09-07 21:41UTC. After41 identified that norm convergence does not control unbounded energy, investigate a local commutator trial estimate for the actual finite-PW charged sector. Candidate was shared with native for a separate full proof before either completed derivation was read.
+
+Use the finite-cutoff neutral FULL-carrier ground from34, gauge-invariant in its uniform weak window. Replacement of one link with its vacuum should imply <K_e><=8v, because only four nonnegative face potentials bounded by2v change. For a distinct d-link path, C=PWP has retained norm q>=1-E_path/e_R. The Rayleigh commutator subtracts the neutral energy before bounding, avoiding volume-sized E0 errors. The full kinetic commutator has trace expectation4d/a and norm bounded by4d/a+4sqrt(d E_path/a). Projection error then costs sqrt(E_path/e_R) times that norm. Far-face compressed potentials commute exactly with C. A touching-face commutator factors through discarded sectors and should cost at most2v(sqrt(E_face/e_R)+sqrt(E_path/e_R)), with E_face<=32v and at most4d touching faces. Check this is actual PW fusion and not mere small output norm. Seek a uniform-in-ambient-volume upper energy bound converging to4d/a for fixed path and R growing. Do not claim fixedR uniformity in arbitrary distance, a continuum limit, or axiomatic dynamics selection.
+
+Prospective controls, if the proof survives: exact constants/Casimir derivative identity, face incidence counts including boundaries, cutoff shell minima and uniform error budget, an adverse showing far-face naive energy comparison scales with ambient volume, and an actual small PW energy fixture if tractable. Failures remain evidence; no fitted threshold.
